 "text": "Hey, nice to have you here. How are you? The simplest way is to lower the seat until your arms and the saddle are comfortable. Then you add pads if needed. Your legs should nearly be straight. Alright. Your legs should nearly be straight when you pedalling at the highest point. Move the seat up a little and try again. That' a good thing. That's the highest point of the pedal under normal riding. If your knees are still hurting, try a different bike, or get a bike fit at a bike shop. Most road bikes are designed to get you close. If you still can't, mountain bikes have higher seats for people with short legs.",
